            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgBingZhao0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgBingZhao0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Longquan kiln complex, diameter: 35.2 cm, late 14th to early 15th century, from the Vohemar site, Madagascar (Musée d’Histoire naturelle de Nîmes). All rights reserved to Dr. Bing Zhou, who has kindly permitted the use of these photographs for educational purposes. (<htcite0>)</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Conteúdo relacionado:</b><ul><li>Famílias: Grande Zimbábue - civilização construída pelo povo Shona, um dos grupos falantes de línguas bantu, no Zimbábue (<htcite1>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgBZ0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgBZ0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Jingdezhen kiln complex and southern China (Zhongguo 中國), 11th to early 13th century, proven from the Sanje ya Kati site, Kilwa-Masoko, Tanzania. All rights reserved to Dr. Bing Zhou, who has kindly permitted the use of these photographs for educational purposes. (<htcite2>)</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Conteúdo relacionado:</b><ul><li>Famílias: Grande Zimbábue - civilização construída pelo povo Shona, um dos grupos falantes de línguas bantu, no Zimbábue (<htcite3>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
